# Auth Pages — Agent Rules

**Full spec:** [docs/auth-feature.md](../../docs/auth-feature.md)  
**Global rules:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md)

## Before coding

1. Read `docs/auth-feature.md` and `AGENTS.md`
2. Confirm guest vs required auth and whether design images exist
3. Do not add auth backend libraries without user approval

## Architecture

- Routes live in `src/app/(auth)/` — screens compose components only
- Mock auth via Zustand + AsyncStorage (reuse `safeStorage` pattern from `use-app-store.ts`)
- Types in `src/types/` — no `any`
- Validation in `src/lib/auth-validation.ts` — pure functions

## UI

- NativeWind v5 for styling; StyleSheet for SafeAreaView, KeyboardAvoidingView, ScrollView contentContainerStyle, TextInput platform props, shadows
- Icons in `src/components/icons.tsx` only — no emoji, no inline SVG
- Images via `src/constants/images.ts`
- Match provided designs pixel-perfectly; otherwise follow onboarding/profile patterns (purple CTA, rounded-2xl, Poppins)

## Store

- `isAuthenticated`, `user`, `registeredUsers` for demo persistence
- On login/sign-up: sync `userRole` with `useAppStore`
- Logout clears session, not onboarding

## Done when

- Login + sign-up work end-to-end with persistence
- Header/profile use real user data (not hardcoded "Dara")
- `npm run lint` passes
- Manual QA from docs/auth-feature.md completed
